# Application Kconfig for the PQC benchmark.
# A Kconfig file in the application root becomes the root of the Kconfig tree, so it MUST
# source the Zephyr Kconfig first (keeps every normal symbol available), then add ours.
source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config PQC_WX
	bool "Apply our own boot-time W^X (RP2350 Hazard3 PMP / ESP32-S3 PMS)"
	default n
	help
	  For the two cores whose memory protection is NOT Zephyr's MPU driver. When y, main()
	  applies W^X once at boot, before any benchmark command:
	    hz3 (RP2350 Hazard3): LOCKED NAPOT PMP entries -- relocated crypto code R+X,
	      relocated crypto tables R only, rest of SRAM R+W no-exec, flash XIP R+X
	      (RP2350 erratum E6 R<->X swap applied). The RP2350 port enables no Zephyr PMP,
	      and Zephyr's generic PMP driver cannot express this policy on this core (its
	      no-execute background would be broken by E6; it knows no relocated blocks).
	    lx7 (ESP32-S3): PMS via Espressif's header-only memprot_ll helpers -- IRAM code R+X,
	      the crypto tables block in DRAM R only (DRAM0 split lines D_0/D_1), rest of DRAM
	      R+W, no execute from the data side.
	  Set in the hz3 and ESP32 board confs so flash AND hybrid images are protected, matching
	  the Arm cores (Zephyr MPU on in every build). The firmware reports what is live as wx=.
	  Ignored on Cortex-M.

config PQC_FETCHTEST
	bool "Arm diagnostic: instruction-fetch cost from flash vs SRAM (console 'fetchtest')"
	default n
	help
	  Diagnostic image only, never a measured image. Adds small timing kernels to main.c, each
	  compiled twice (flash .text and __ramfunc SRAM), plus the same load/store loops with the
	  data in other SRAM banks, to find out why the PSoC 62 Cortex-M4 runs the crypto SLOWER
	  from SRAM than from flash, and whether the RP2350 Cortex-M33 shows the same effect.
	  Cortex-M4 and Cortex-M33 only.

config PQC_CRYPTO_IN_IRAM
	bool "Place the wolfSSL crypto working set in internal SRAM (IRAM/DRAM)"
	default n
	help
	  Placement experiment (RQ1, ESP32-S3). When y, the SoC linker pulls the wolfSSL crypto
	  objects' .text/.literal into IRAM and their .rodata into DRAM instead of executing from
	  flash via the instruction cache. Requires the matching esp32s3/default.ld input-section
	  patch (guarded on this symbol). Ignored on non-Xtensa targets.
